A paper-native route is emerging from Section 6: line graphs of multigraphs are claw-free, and the paper explicitly identifies the 5-cycle with triple edges as the sharp \(\Delta=8\) obstruction. Raising each cycle edge to multiplicity four moves the same native object into \(\Delta=11\), where a 10-color witness exists. I’m stress-testing whether the resulting “twin-clique cycle” coloring is genuinely nontrivial under Track B, rather than trusting the large raw answer space.
