The initial exact G4 loop was correct but wasteful: almost every candidate already fails at the first pair of incident bundles, yet it was materializing all 236 entries before checking. I’m replacing that with lazy sampling from the identical declared distribution—still 200,000 structure-aware candidates, but it stops drawing a candidate once its failure is already certain.
