codex
Built the Track B generator and verified every local gate.

The family uses fourfold multicycle edges: their line graphs are claw-free with \(\Delta=11\), no \(K_{11}\), and admit constructed 10-colorings, matching the paper’s Section 6 regime ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.1269)).

Key results:

- G1–G9(c): pass
- Guessing: 0/200,000
- Exact log-density: −67.35
- Reference DP: 220,134 operations
- Compact route: 236 placements
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each
- Answer: 1,181 characters, 236 elements

Files:

- [gen_1206_1269.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/gen_1206_1269.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1206.1269/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only blocker is external: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” for every vendor. The transcripts contain those script-authored errors, correctly counted as zero valid attempts. Consequently the README marks the result not yet shippable. Restoring OpenRouter quota and rerunning `harden.py` is the remaining step.
